LOCAL5="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries are missing: dpkg has i386 (for Steam, Wine and 32-bit games) and NVIDIA's driver %s is installed, but not its i386 libraries at that version (%s), so 32-bit programs get no NVIDIA OpenGL, Vulkan or CUDA. Repair installs them (sudo sparky-stereo-hardware --nvidia-i386)."
LOCAL6="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries (%s) could not be installed: %s exited %s (its output is kept with this problem). Fix what it names, then repair again (sudo sparky-stereo-hardware --nvidia-i386)."
LOCAL7="There is no NVIDIA driver to match: nvidia-driver-libs is not installed for amd64, so NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries have no version to follow. Run Hardware Setup to install NVIDIA's driver."
LOCAL8="dpkg has no i386, so NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries are not needed: nothing was installed."
LOCAL9="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries"
LOCAL10="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries could not be installed by themselves after the apt run that needed them: %s exited %s. Its output is kept with this problem and says why (for example no network, or a repository that did not answer). Repair installs them again (sudo sparky-stereo-hardware --nvidia-i386)."
LOCAL11="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries are installed (%s, at %s): they were installed by themselves after the apt run that needed them, so Steam, Wine and 32-bit games get NVIDIA's OpenGL, Vulkan and CUDA."
LOCAL12="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries (%s) at %s are installed by themselves when this apt run ends (%s); the session is told when they are in."
LOCAL13="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries are missing (%s, at %s) and cannot be installed by themselves here: %s. Repair installs them (sudo sparky-stereo-hardware --nvidia-i386)."
LOCAL14="They are installed by themselves when the next apt run that installs packages ends, once apt-get update has read i386's package lists; Repair installs them now."
LOCAL15="NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries (%s) at %s cannot be installed: apt finds no way to install them (apt-get --simulate install exited %s). Its output is kept with this problem and names what is missing (for example that version gone from the repositories, or i386's package lists not read yet). Repair reads the package lists and installs them (sudo sparky-stereo-hardware --nvidia-i386)."
LOCAL16="Installing NVIDIA's 32-bit libraries. If another apt or dpkg operation is running, this repair waits for it to finish."
LOCAL17="Bluetooth voice"
LOCAL18="The Bluetooth adapter %s cannot carry a headset's microphone or calls: it gives the computer no voice channel, so a microphone through it stays silent. Music and other sound through it still work, and other Bluetooth adapters are not affected. For a microphone or calls, use another Bluetooth adapter or a headset on a cable or USB."
